 r←ref IsValidHandler name;hasResult;valence
⍝ Returns 1 when `name`, as seen from the namespace `ref`, is a function that returns a result
⍝ and can be called monadically: a monadic or an ambivalent function, a dfn for example.
⍝ An empty name is valid, because all handlers except `OnRequest` are optional; the caller checks that one.
⍝ Note that attribute 10 is ¯1 for a shy result.
 :If 0=≢name
     r←1
 :Else
     (hasResult valence)←10 11 ref.⎕ATX name
     r←(0≠hasResult)∧valence∊1 ¯2
 :EndIf
⍝Done
